Setting Up the Project
======================

Backend (Django + SQLite)
-------------------------

Python 3.10-3.12. Use 3.12 if you want face recognition: TensorFlow has no
3.13 wheels yet.

    cd Backend
    python3.12 -m venv .venv
    source .venv/bin/activate
    pip install -r requirements.txt

    cp .env.example .env          # then edit it
    python manage.py migrate
    python manage.py createsuperuser   # this account gets the "admin" role
    python manage.py runserver

No MySQL, no cmake, and no dlib compile any more. The database is a SQLite file
at Backend/db.sqlite3 (override with DJANGO_DB_PATH).

Face recognition (optional)
---------------------------

The face stack is a separate install because it is a large download (~500 MB)
and takes a while to pull the model weights on first use:

    pip install -r requirements-face.txt

Then set FACE_RECOGNITION_ENABLED=true in Backend/.env.

With it disabled, the server runs fine and the face endpoints return HTTP 503.
They deliberately refuse rather than waving attendance through — turning face
recognition off must never mean "everyone passes".

To use a different library, add a backend class to
Face_Recognation/services.py. Nothing outside that file needs to change.

Roles
-----

Three roles: student, teacher, admin.

  - Public signup always creates a student. The role is never taken from the
    request body.
  - createsuperuser creates an admin.
  - An admin promotes people, either in the Django admin at /admin/ or with:

        PATCH /api/Auth/users/<username>/role   {"role": "teacher"}

  - Students must enrol a face (POST /api/Face_Recog/register_image) before
    they can mark attendance.

Running the tests
-----------------

    cd Backend
    python manage.py test

These cover the role matrix, course ownership, and the attendance rules
(geofence, session window, duplicate marking, face match). They stub the face
model out, so they run without the TensorFlow install.

Frontend (React)
----------------

    cd frontend
    npm install
    npm start

Copy frontend/.env.example to frontend/.env if the API is not on
http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/.

NOTE: the frontend has not been migrated to the reworked API yet. The axios
client and the auth hooks are updated; the components still expect the old
request/response shapes, so the app will not work end to end until they are
brought across.
